ALGORITHM: Minimum Path Sum

1. Start.

2. Get the number of rows:
       m = number of rows

   Get the number of columns:
       n = number of columns

3. Traverse every cell of the grid.

4. For the first cell:
       If i = 0 and j = 0:
           Keep the value unchanged.

5. For cells in the first row:
       If i = 0:
           grid[i][j] = grid[i][j] + grid[i][j-1]

6. For cells in the first column:
       If j = 0:
           grid[i][j] = grid[i][j] + grid[i-1][j]

7. For all other cells:
       grid[i][j] = grid[i][j] + min(grid[i-1][j],
                                     grid[i][j-1])

8. Continue until the bottom-right cell is reached.

9. Return:
       grid[m-1][n-1]

TIME COMPLEXITY:
O(m × n)

SPACE COMPLEXITY:
O(1)
